# With the input trace on (androidboot.hardware.dsa_input_trace=1 on the kernel command line),
# every app's main thread logs each message it takes 16 ms or more to handle ("Slow dispatch"),
# naming the handler and the callback, and the first message it starts 16 ms or more late
# ("Slow delivery"). A frame, an activity launch and a click are each one such message, so the
# log shows where the main thread's time went between a press and the frame that answers it.
# Off by default: every app logs more. The lines stay in logd's memory, and `dsa logcat` reads
# them.
#
# It is a system script, not a vendor one, because init runs vendor scripts in a context that
# may not set log properties. Each app reads the property when its main thread starts.
on property:ro.boot.hardware.dsa_input_trace=1
    setprop log.looper.any.main.slow 16
